// ---- inputs: syntax_0 … syntax_24, base_server_plan.py's named nodes but comments and string parts ----
// Each shard captures NODE and, optionally, PARENT (`inside`, stopBy neighbor: the direct parent: `child`) and the
// first child in each of 11 fields (`has`, stopBy neighbor, field F: `field`), so the atoms export nothing. A shard
// projects the field columns its kinds have (call: function, arguments; attribute: object, attribute;
// keyword_argument: name, value; assignment/augmented_assignment: left, right, type; definitions: name, return_type;
// the other named shards' kinds have none of the 11; the catch-all shards project all 11), so they are one relation.
.decl syntax_rows_0(n: node)
